TEST 38097 -- MRP ring with DUT as MRC
===========================================================================
Run: 2026-09-30 15:36-15:56 NZDT, tb470, hand-driven (no framework script), queue row 9.
Tester: bench-runner. Case text: AWPTCM-T38097 (ck.db zephyr_cases), 9 steps.

VERDICT: PASS -- labelled CONFOUNDED, on the ring-closure loops only. Those come
from sw1's MRM, not from the DUT. The proof is below.

  The DUT, as MRC, did everything the case asks. Its config was accepted. The ring
  is operational after the save. When its forwarding port was shut, traffic
  recovered on the other link in 92-98 ms. After the restore one port was blocked
  again and traffic continued. After save and reboot the DUT loaded its config
  without errors, rejoined the ring as MRC, and traffic flowed again (180 s
  steady state clean).
  CONFOUND: every ring CLOSURE looped VLAN 1 for 26-40 ms (4 of 4: the role-swap
  close, both restores, the post-boot ring-up). The loops come from the partner
  MRM, the IE520-sa on the same build. Its log shows the same false
  `CHK_RC -> CHK_RO evt=MRP_ProtEvTestTimerExpired` -> "Ring opened" that T38093
  graded FAIL on the stack MRM. The DUT's MRC state machine is correct: it holds a
  returning port (DE_IDLE -> PT) and forwards it only on the MRM's
  TopologyChangeInd. So the DUT's MRC role is not the cause. The MRM defect is
  graded in 38093-fail.log.

DUT / TOPOLOGY
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  DUT      IE520-stk (stk_a) = MRC, members 1/3/4, master member 3 before and after its
           reboot (prio 128 all, lowest MAC wins). Ring ports on TWO members:
             port1.0.13 [m1] (copper AT-SP10TM, a-1000) and port4.0.26 [m4] (fibre SX).
  sw1      IE520-sa = MRM (role manager).  sw2: NONE -- one MRP-capable partner; step 4
           not run.  Ring 1, VLAN 1, profile 200ms (default) on both.
  traffic  as 38093-fail.log: 4 x 500 pps flows eth3 -> x230 -> stack sa2 -> ring -> SA ->
           eth2 and back. Transit proof (evidence/38097/s6-mac-u5.out, -u3.out): stack
           learns eth2 (..7717) on port1.0.13, SA learns eth3 (..7718) on port1.0.13.
  Gate     row 9 gate 14:32-14:34 (38093-fail.log); re-verified 14:58 (evidence/row9/resume-*).

